  "baseRefName": "main",
  "body": "## Summary\n- add an opt-in, private-repository-only managed Codex auth flow for GitHub-hosted runners\n- encrypt `auth.json` with AES-256-GCM, keep the key in an Actions secret, and serialize refresh/write-back with a repository-variable lock\n- restore before Codex runs, persist after session backup, remove plaintext auth, and report the mode during onboarding\n- add a seed command that selects hosted runners and owner-only trigger access\n\n## Security\n- plaintext Codex auth is never stored in a repository variable or committed\n- encrypted state is bound to the target repository\n- runtime rejects public repositories and self-hosted runners\n- the App needs Variables read/write, not Secrets write\n\n## Validation\n- `npm --prefix .agent test`\n- 761 runtime tests passed\n- 90 workflow tests passed\n- docs and shell checks passed\n\nThis follows OpenAI managed CI auth guidance for trusted private automation while keeping `OPENAI_API_KEY` as the recommended default.",
